    description: "Concept DOI: cites all versions of this work."
abstract: "Reproducible measurement of Portugal's general-government interest burden from the harmonised Eurostat ESA 2010 record for 1995-2025, and of how quickly a rate shock reaches it. Keeps national-accounts interest expense, the GDP-normalised burden, the average financing cost of the stock, the debt-dynamics rate and the benchmark yield on new debt as distinct quantities; publishes an exact two-factor decomposition of the burden change and a euro-area comparison with a stated eligibility rule. A companion study asks what weighted average maturity does and does not determine about pass-through speed. Contains the pipeline, the generated tables and figures, and two working papers built from them."
